Evaluate and optimize AI agents — baseline scoring and iterative improvement.

When run without a subcommand, submits an optimization job.
Use --eval to reuse an agent-targeted evaluation from an azure.ai.eval service,
or --eval-config to select an evaluation configuration file.
Use --config for an optimization request file (YAML or JSON).
Omitted optional optimization settings use service defaults.
Legacy agent eval.yaml files are not supported.

Usage
  azd ai agent optimize [agent-name] [flags]
  azd ai agent optimize [command]

Available Commands
  apply  : Apply optimized candidate configuration locally to your azd project.
  cancel : Cancel a running optimization job.
  deploy : Deploy a winning optimization candidate as a new agent version via the API.
  list   : List recent optimization runs.
  status : Check the status of an optimization job.

Flags
  -a, --agent string            : Agent service name from azure.yaml, or Foundry agent name outside a project
  -c, --config string           : Optimization request file (YAML or JSON)
  -d, --dataset string          : Local JSONL file or registered dataset as name:version
      --endpoint string         : Optimization service endpoint (for local dev)
      --eval string             : Evaluation name to reuse from the selected evaluation configuration
      --eval-config string      : Evaluation configuration from 'azd ai eval init'
  -m, --eval-model string       : Model for evaluation (required)
      --evaluator stringArray   : Built-in or custom evaluator name (repeatable; required when not set in config)
      --max-candidates int      : Maximum number of optimization candidates to generate (must be >= 1; service default when omitted)
      --no-wait                 : Submit job and return immediately without waiting for completion
      --optimize-model string   : Model for optimization reasoning (gpt-5 family recommended; required)
      --poll-interval int       : Polling interval in seconds (default 10)
  -p, --project-endpoint string : Foundry project endpoint URL

Global Flags
  -C, --cwd string         : Sets the current working directory
      --debug              : Enables debug and diagnostics logging
  -e, --environment string : The name of the environment to use
  -h, --help               : help for optimize
      --no-prompt          : Runs without prompts. Uses existing values; fails if any required value or decision cannot be resolved automatically.
  -o, --output string      : The output format (supported: json, table) (default "table")

Examples
  Optimize (auto-detect agent from azd project)
    azd ai agent optimize

  Optimize a specific agent
    azd ai agent optimize my-agent

  Full control via config file
    azd ai agent optimize --config spec.yaml

  Reuse an evaluation from the new evaluation workflow
    azd ai agent optimize --eval quality --optimize-model optimizer-deployment

  Subcommands
    azd ai agent optimize status <id> --watch
    azd ai agent optimize list
    azd ai agent optimize cancel <id>
    azd ai agent optimize deploy --candidate <id>

Use azd ai agent optimize [command] --help to view examples and more information about a specific command.
